<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Grand Palace of Bangkok</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand Palace is a complex of royal buildings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, built from 1782 on Rattanakosin Island by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Rama I</a>, founder of the Chakri dynasty, when he moved the capital from Thonburi. Surrounded by walls, it housed the royal court and government until the 20th century and includes the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-phra-kaew">Wat Phra Kaew</a>, home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha">Emerald Buddha</a>. It is still used for state ceremonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-palace.jpg" alt="Grand Palace" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Preecha.MJ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0005574_-_Wat_Phra_Kaew_006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
